# SERVER_PUBLIC_IP stands for the server's public address. The live copy on the server, /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, carries the real one.
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile - AS IT IS TODAY, before anything changes.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE YOU USE THIS FILE FOR A ROLLBACK.
#
# This file is a readable copy of today's Caddy setup. It says the same thing
# as the live file. It may not be byte-for-byte identical to it, because the
# live file was read as a summary and not copied.
#
# So this file is NOT the rollback copy.
#
# The real rollback copy is the one deploy/scripts/backup_before_cutover.sh
# takes straight off the server, before anything changes. It lands at
#   /home/ubuntu/backups/<timestamp>/etc/caddy/Caddyfile
# and deploy/scripts/rollback.sh restores that one.
#
# This file is here for two reasons. First, so you can read today's routing
# without logging in. Second, as a last resort if a backup is ever lost.
#
# The three site blocks below belong to Harrier. Harrier is a separate app on
# 127.0.0.1:8400. Nothing in this deployment touches it.

{
	default_sni SERVER_PUBLIC_IP
}

https://SERVER_PUBLIC_IP:8080 {
	tls {
		issuer acme {
			profile shortlived
		}
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8400
}

https://harrier.141-147-81-233.sslip.io:8080 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8400
}

http://harrier.141-147-81-233.sslip.io {
	redir https://harrier.141-147-81-233.sslip.io:8080{uri} permanent
}
